{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_pc_03_draft_four_coupling_schemes", "label": "The four coupling schemes as physical recoupling chains", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PC-03-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The schemes are physical, not notational: each applies where its couplings are the strong ones - LS when the electrostatic term dominates, jj when spin-orbit does, jK when the outer electron is loosely bound and its own spin-orbit is the weakest interaction and so is coupled last, which is why jK is the scheme high Rydberg states realise."}, {"id": "recovered_pc_03_draft_jk_exact_bound", "label": "jK's exact final bound |2J - 2K| <= 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PC-03-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the outer electron's spin is 1/2 the final triangle K + s2 = J degenerates to a mutual bound that closes, so jK reaches an exact bound where the other three schemes do not - an advantage of the scheme in this index specifically."}, {"id": "recovered_pc_03_draft_racah_recoupling", "label": "Racah 1942 recoupling algebra", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recovered/PC-03-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_pc_03_draft_cowan_andrew", "label": "Cowan & Andrew 1965, the four pure coupling types", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recovered/PC-03-draft.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_pc_03_draft_four_coupling_schemes", "target": "recovered_pc_03_draft_jk_exact_bound", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PC-03-draft.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {